{"hookSpecificOutput":{"additionalContext":"Jalon: this conversation holds about 212K tokens of context. Answer the user's message first.\nThen end your reply with a short section written as a Markdown blockquote (every line starts with \"> \"), whose first words are\n**Jalon** —, in the language the user writes in; it recommends ONE option:\n1. New session: the latest request starts a task unrelated to the earlier work. Say so in one line.\n2. Handoff: the same task continues and much state must carry over. Give the section first, then write\n   .jalon/handoffs/2026-10-12/0900-1riq1ius-<short-slug>.md, in the language the user writes in. Its first line is \"Session: s1\". Then: goal, decisions and why, what was dropped and why, current state (what was checked, with the\n   command or test run and its result in a few words; what was not: ideas, assumptions, untested fixes), the user's latest request and the answer this reply gives it, files involved, next steps (proposals to confirm with the user, not orders), pitfalls and what not to redo.\n   Never list an outward action (push, pull or merge request, API call, message to a person or another session) as a thing\n   to do: at most as waiting for the user's OK. State the facts the next steps need from outside sources\n   (tickets, docs, web pages, logs): a new session cannot see them. No raw tool output. Then give the user the lines to copy, in a code block: /clear, then @.jalon/handoffs/2026-10-12/0900-1riq1ius-<short-slug>.md (the full path) followed by a request, in the user's language,\n   to read it, sum up its goal, state and next step in three lines, keeping what was not checked marked as not\n   checked, then wait for the user's request without checking again the state it describes; the request names no task\n   or next step.\n   If a skill or command you were given defines your role for the ongoing work, whether it was invoked at the start\n   or later, say so in the handoff and list any background task to restart; then the second line is that command\n   followed by the handoff's full path as plain text and a request, in the user's language,\n   to read it, sum up its goal, state and next step in three lines, keeping what was not checked marked as not\n   checked, then wait for the user's request without checking again the state it describes; the request names no task\n   or next step. Do not re-invoke a skill\n   used once for a side task.\n3. Compact: the same task continues with little state to carry. Give one ready line, in a code block: /compact <what to keep;\n   what to drop>.\nWhile background work you started that will report back (agents, background commands) is still running, do not recommend\na new session or /clear: its result would reach a conversation that lost why it was started, or end with this session.\nWrite option 2's handoff now, while the whole conversation is in context, with the running work and what to do with its\nresult in its current state. Then recommend a compact whose line keeps the running work, what to do with its result, and\nthe handoff's full path as the record to update when the work reports. Then give, in a code block, the line the user\ncopies once the work has reported: a request, in the user's language, to update that handoff with what changed and give the lines to resume from it.\nKeep the section under 10 lines, apart from the handoff file. Give it in this reply only: do not repeat it in later replies.","hookEventName":"UserPromptSubmit"},"systemMessage":"Jalon: context at 212K tokens, a reset proposal follows the answer."}
